From d14bab8cfaae34fa9541e5bfa2eb19d505790892 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Levine <blahm1d@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 19:01:07 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] core: P0016 - wire the external LINT1 pin (DMA-done ->
 blit-queue pump)

The Y-unit game's per-frame drawing is a blit QUEUE pumped by the INT1
ISR (vector -> ffe00000): the ISR feeds one blit to the DMA engine;
blit completion asserts LINT1 in hardware (MAME dma_callback:
set_input_line(0, ASSERT_LINE)); any DMA COMMAND write clears it
(dma_w: CLEAR_LINE). Without the pin, the title task submitted exactly
ONE blit (the top strip of the version-info rectangle, confirmed by the
cabinet owner) and yielded forever -- pixel-static screen through 400+
frames while everything else (scheduler, inputs, coin credit) ran fine.

Fix: new core input `lint1_in`, mirrored into INTPEND.X1P by io_regs
per the UG (X1P reflects the pin; not clearable via INTPEND writes).
The mirror uses (lint1_in === 1'b1) so ~99 legacy core TBs with the
port unconnected keep working unchanged.

VERIFIED (32M-cycle integrated run): blit pump runs, screens advance,
coin -> credit, START -> game state 0x30->0x10->0x18, and the post-
START frame shows REAL GAMEPLAY (player sprite, HUD panels, icons
matching MAME's arena). No illegal opcodes; all regression TBs PASS.

