+---
+
+## P0016 — external interrupt pin LINT1 wired (DMA-done -> blit-queue pump)
+
+**Status:** ✅ APPLIED + VERIFIED 2026-07-05. `grep -rn P0016 rtl/`.
+
+**Applied edits:**
+- `rtl/core/tms34010_core.sv`: new input port `lint1_in` (external LINT1 pin level),
+  passed to `u_io_regs`.
+- `rtl/io/tms34010_io_regs.sv`: new input `lint1_in`; INTPEND.X1P (bit 1) is a live
+  MIRROR of the pin (per the 1988 UG §8.3 X1P reflects the pin and is not clearable
+  by writing INTPEND) — OR-folded into both the `intpend_o` tap and CPU reads of
+  INTPEND. The mirror uses `(lint1_in === 1'b1)` so the ~99 legacy core TBs that
+  leave the new port unconnected ('z) keep working unchanged (unconnected = not
+  asserted; synthesis treats === as ==).
+- Wrapper `rtl/yunit/yunit_memsys.sv`: new output `int1` = `yunit_dma.blit_irq`
+  (which has implemented the exact MAME semantics since Phase 0: SET on blit
+  completion, CLEARED by any DMA COMMAND write — midyunit_v.cpp dma_callback
+  370-374 `set_input_line(0, ASSERT_LINE)` / dma_w 433 `CLEAR_LINE`). 20
+  integrated TBs wire memsys.int1 -> core.lint1_in.
+
+**Problem.** The Y-unit game's per-frame drawing is a blit QUEUE pumped by the INT1
+ISR (vector 0xFFFFFFC0 -> `ffe00000`): the ISR writes one queued blit to the DMA
+registers; when the blitter finishes, the HARDWARE asserts LINT1; the ISR pumps the
+next blit; the final COMMAND write clears the line. The 2026-07-04 measurement
+"Smash T.V. is poll-driven, no interrupts needed" was TRUE for the POST/self-test
+(which polls COMMAND bit15) but WRONG for the game proper. With no LINT1 wiring the
+title task submits exactly ONE blit and then yields forever waiting for the pump.
+
+**Evidence (measured).** The boot's cooperative scheduler is fully healthy (walker
+probe: list walk + JUMP-A7 dispatch verified; BOTH tasks entered — title task
+`fff596f0`, service task `ffeaf490`). The title task ran its VRAM clear (183,958 CPU
+VRAM writes), drew ONE item — a single orange line = the top strip of the version-
+info rectangle (confirmed by the cabinet owner: the real game shows an orange
+version box after ROM checks, then high scores) — then parked at resume `fff59890`
+re-sleeping forever. All VRAM activity stops at ~6M cycles; the screen is pixel-
+static through 400+ frames, a coin, and START. GOs/blits: none after the first.
+MAME's `dma_callback` names the missing hardware: DMA-done asserts input line 0.
+
+**VERIFIED (tb_yunit_state, 32M cycles).** With LINT1 wired the blit pump runs and
+THE GAME PLAYS END-TO-END: screens advance (frame dumps now differ per phase), coin
+→ coin sound + credit, START → game-state `@10865A0` 0x30→0x10→0x18 (GAME), and the
+post-START frame shows REAL GAMEPLAY (player sprite, HUD/score panels matching
+MAME's arena layout, weapon/prize icons) with the CPU actively in the pump ISR.
+No illegal opcodes. All regression TBs PASS (the ~99 legacy core TBs run unchanged
+with the pin unconnected, thanks to the === guard).
